+  >    preserve class identity at once.** There is no uplift term, so the process's steady state is
+  >    a peneplain and any concavity the depth law shows is a transient of the carrier it started
+  >    from, not an attractor the incision reaches. On steep classes the 25 m `incision_cap_m` then
+  >    becomes the carve outright: **65–82% of channel cells sit at the cap** under
+  >    `incision_mode = "profile"` (against 0.06–2.5% under the default per-cell `"depth"` law),
+  >    so `max` incision is fully censored and the cap constant is the only depth knob left that
+  >    matters.
