+  >    ships disabled.** `incise.profile_incision` solves the same stream-power law implicitly along
+  >    the D8 receiver tree (`z_new = z - K_dt·A^m·((z_new - z_new(receiver))/dist)^n`, one
+  >    downstream-to-upstream pass), giving `z ≥ z(receiver)` by construction — no carve-created
+  >    pits, no single cell punching a shaft through the tile. Measured on the three exemplar tiles:
+  >    at `K_dt = 4.5` with a regional-slope energy scale (`profile_regional_s_ref = 0.2`, the
+  >    solve's stand-in for the missing uplift term), alpine theta moves **0.040 → 0.146** (r² 0.97,
